@ref Decree 67/2023 Article 17(1)(a)-(h)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ceiling of Article 17(1)`
`Article 17(1) — the ceilings` MEANS
    --                                    head                                                                              percent, the base includes the balance of earlier years
    LIST (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(a) humanitarian support, and repaying advances`,                                 30, TRUE),
         (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(b) works and equipment to prevent and limit losses and road accidents`,          15, TRUE),
         (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(c) propaganda and education on road safety and the compulsory motor insurance`,  17, TRUE),
         (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(d) support for the police`,                                                      10, FALSE),
         (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(dd) rewards for achievement`,                                                     5, FALSE),
         (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(e) the database of the compulsory motor insurance`,                              10, FALSE),
         (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(g) the ASEAN compulsory motor insurance programme`,                               5, FALSE),
         (`A ceiling of Article 17(1)` OF `(h) managing the Fund`,                                                            8, FALSE)

@ref Decree 67/2023 Article 17(1); fork V12
GIVEN receipts IS A LIST OF `A receipt of the Fund`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 17(1) — the year's contributions paid into the Fund, among` receipts MEANS
    `Article 15 — the Fund's receipts from` `contributions of the insurers` `among` receipts

@ref Decree 67/2023 Article 17(1)(a)-(h)
GIVEN head          IS A `A head of the Fund's spending`
      contributions IS A NUMBER
      balance       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 17(1) — the most the Fund may spend in a year under` head `, on contributions of` contributions `and a balance of earlier years of` balance MEANS
    sum (map `the ceiling of the row` (filter (GIVEN row YIELD row's head EQUALS head) `Article 17(1) — the ceilings`))
    WHERE
        `the ceiling of the row` row MEANS
            IF   row's `the base includes the balance of earlier years`
            THEN (contributions PLUS balance) TIMES (row's percent)%
            ELSE contributions TIMES (row's percent)%

-- Which heads a year's spending took past their ceilings.
@ref Decree 67/2023 Article 17(1)(a)-(h)
GIVEN spending      IS A LIST OF `A year's spending under a head`
      contributions IS A NUMBER
      balance       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A head of the Fund's spending`
`Article 17(1) — the heads overspent by` spending `, on contributions of` contributions `and a balance of earlier years of` balance MEANS
    map (GIVEN row YIELD row's head) (filter `overspent` `Article 17(1) — the ceilings`)
    WHERE
        `spent under` head MEANS sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's amount) (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s's head EQUALS head) spending))
        `overspent` row MEANS
            `spent under` (row's head) GREATER THAN `Article 17(1) — the most the Fund may spend in a year under` (row's head) `, on contributions of` contributions `and a balance of earlier years of` balance

-- Point (a), the carry-over: where the Fund has spent in the year all it may spend on
-- humanitarian support, the files not yet settled pass to the next year's humanitarian
-- support. Fork V24: a file is paid whole or carried whole; one that would take point (a)'s
-- spending past its ceiling is carried. The paragraph names only humanitarian support files,
-- not the repayment of advances, though both are spent under point (a) (finding R7).
