GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 17(1)(i) — the most that may be spent from the balance of earlier years on points (d) to (h), on premiums of` `the premiums the contributions are computed on` MEANS
    (`the premiums the contributions are computed on` TIMES 1%) TIMES (`the sum of the rates of points (d) to (h)`)%
    WHERE
        `the sum of the rates of points (d) to (h)` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN row YIELD row's percent) (filter (GIVEN row YIELD NOT (row's `the base includes the balance of earlier years`)) `Article 17(1) — the ceilings`))

§§ `Article 17(2) — priorities`

-- Inert: the Vietnam Insurance Association gives priority to humanitarian support, prevention
-- and propaganda, in keeping with the Fund's purpose. It names no measure of priority and
-- decides no case.
